{"nodes": [{"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_recursive_proof_composition", "label": "Recursive Proof Composition Outline", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three-chapter treatment (survey, folding deep dive, applications); historical arc theme: each generation moved more work out of the recursive step."}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_ivc", "label": "Incrementally Verifiable Computation (IVC)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two independence conditions \u2014 update work and verify work independent of step count \u2014 distinguish IVC from naive prove-the-whole-history approaches."}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_pcd", "label": "Proof-Carrying Data (PCD)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Generalizes IVC from a chain to a DAG across mutually distrusting parties; IVC is the path-graph special case; compliance predicates define local correctness."}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_three_core_capabilities", "label": "Compression, Incrementality, Composability", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Recursion buys three distinct things and conflating them causes confusion; each maps to different applications and constructions."}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_succinctness_threshold", "label": "Succinctness Threshold", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The verifier circuit must be asymptotically and concretely smaller than the statements proven or recursion diverges; accumulation and folding deliberately relax this by deferring expensive checks."}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_full_recursion", "label": "Full Recursion", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Embed the complete inner verifier in-circuit; the field-mismatch problem (base vs scalar field) is classically fixed with a cycle of elliptic curves."}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_atomic_accumulation", "label": "Atomic Accumulation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Halo's insight: the expensive MSM check need not run in-circuit each step \u2014 fold it into a running accumulator verified once at the end; this removed trusted setup from practical recursion and is the conceptual bridge to folding."}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_folding_schemes", "label": "Folding Schemes", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Reduce checking two instances to one; deliberately weaker than an argument of knowledge because weaker primitives admit simpler, faster realizations. Costs: no standalone mid-computation proof, mandatory additively homomorphic commitments, final compression SNARK required."}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_stark_recursion", "label": "STARK Recursion", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Small fields (Goldilocks, BabyBear, Mersenne-31), algebraic hashes (Poseidon) and lookup arguments made FRI verification in-circuit practical; transparent and plausibly post-quantum."}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_hybrid_pipelines", "label": "Hybrid Proving Pipelines", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Dominant production pattern: parallel STARK prover for bulk execution, recursive STARK aggregation, final SNARK wrap for cheap on-chain verification \u2014 with the uncomfortable tradeoff that the wrapper often reintroduces a trusted setup."}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_curve_cycles", "label": "Elliptic Curve Cycles", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two curves, each one's scalar field equal to the other's base field, alternating per recursion layer to fix the verifier/circuit field mismatch; finding good cycles remains a hard open problem."}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_pasta_curves", "label": "Pasta Curves (Pallas/Vesta)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_halo", "label": "Halo", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Recursive proof composition without a trusted setup, via accumulation of the deferred inner-product-argument check."}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_nova", "label": "Nova", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Reference folding construction: the augmented step circuit verifies the previous fold with two group scalar multiplications and a hash (~10^4 constraints vs 10^6+ for an embedded SNARK verifier)."}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_r1cs", "label": "R1CS", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Naive instances don't fold: the quadratic constraint produces cross terms under random linear combination that satisfy no instance."}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_relaxed_r1cs", "label": "Relaxed R1CS", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Adds scalar u and error vector E (Az . Bz = u*(Cz) + E), shaped exactly to absorb the folding cross terms; relaxation makes the satisfiability set closed under interpolation."}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_pedersen_commitment", "label": "Pedersen Commitments in Folding", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Additive homomorphism lets the verifier fold commitments with two scalar multiplications while the prover folds the vectors; this discrete-log dependence is precisely where post-quantum folding gets stuck."}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_spartan", "label": "Spartan", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Final compression SNARK in the Nova reference implementation; sum-check over multilinear extensions with no FFTs pairs naturally with Nova."}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_fiat_shamir_ivc", "label": "Fiat-Shamir in IVC", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The random-oracle hash runs inside the next step's circuit with adversary-controlled inputs across unbounded depth; recent concrete attacks make this the sharpest theory-practice gap in deployed recursion."}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_extractor_blowup", "label": "Extractor Blowup", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Recursion composes extractors, so knowledge-soundness theorems hold only for constant or logarithmic depth while deployed systems recurse thousands of times."}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_supernova", "label": "SuperNova", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Non-uniform IVC: one running instance per instruction type selected by a program counter, avoiding the universal switch circuit that would reintroduce the costs folding was meant to kill."}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_ccs", "label": "Customizable Constraint Systems (CCS)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Generalizes R1CS, Plonkish and AIR under one umbrella with higher-degree constraints."}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_hypernova", "label": "HyperNova", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Sum-check-based multifolding of CCS keeps verifier work logarithmic as constraint degree grows and avoids committing to cross-term error vectors entirely."}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_protostar", "label": "ProtoStar / ProtoGalaxy", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Folding as a compiler: any special-sound protocol becomes a folding/accumulation scheme, yielding lookups with prover cost independent of table size; ProtoGalaxy folds many instances with sublinear verifier cost."}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_cyclefold", "label": "CycleFold", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The second curve is only needed for a handful of foreign-field group ops, so its circuit shrinks to a single scalar multiplication (~1,500 gates) whose correctness is folded on the primary curve."}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_latticefold", "label": "LatticeFold", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Replaces Pedersen with Ajtai-style lattice commitments for post-quantum folding; core obstacle: lattice commitments are homomorphic only for short vectors and random linear combinations destroy shortness."}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_binding_failures", "label": "Verification-Key Binding Failures", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Real soundness bugs in recursive systems are rarely deep cryptography \u2014 they are binding failures; bind VK hashes into statements, domain-separate transcripts, treat every cross-layer interface as adversarial."}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_mina", "label": "Mina / Coda", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Recursion in its purest form: the entire chain state attested by one constant-size proof updated recursively per block, so anyone verifies from genesis in milliseconds."}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_pickles", "label": "Pickles", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_fractal", "label": "Fractal", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "First transparent, post-quantum recursion via holography."}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_plonky2", "label": "Plonky2", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_aggregation_trees", "label": "Aggregation Trees", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Tree shape is a tuning knob: deeper trees cut per-node prover cost and parallelize; shallower trees cut latency and total work."}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_continuations", "label": "Continuations / Sharding", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The most economically important recursion pattern today: chunk the trace, prove chunks in parallel on GPU clusters, recursively merge with boundary-consistency checks between adjacent chunks."}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_recursion_gap", "label": "Recursion Gap", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The multiplicative overhead of proving a verifier versus just running it; levers include smaller fields, better in-circuit hashes, lookups, and folding's near-elimination of the embedded verifier."}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_rollups", "label": "Rollups and Proof Compression", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The original killer app: recursion aggregates per-batch proofs and compresses the final proof for cheap on-chain verification (the canonical STARK-to-SNARK squeeze)."}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_real_time_proving", "label": "Real-Time L1 Proving", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ethereum L1 zkEVM requires block proofs in ~10-12s, proof size under 300 KiB, and no trusted-setup recursive wrappers; the race went from ~200 GPUs (2025) to 16 GPUs (2026)."}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_sbom_pcd", "label": "SBOM Verification as PCD", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A software bill of materials is a dependency DAG, and dependency DAGs are PCD graphs \u2014 the outline's canonical real-world PCD instance, with one root proof over the transitive closure."}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_zkml", "label": "Verifiable AI (zkML)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Neural networks are chains of structurally similar layers \u2014 exactly IVC's shape; distinguish proof of inference, model provenance, and training (vastly harder)."}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_valiant_ivc_paper", "label": "Valiant, Incrementally Verifiable Computation (TCC 2008)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_chiesa_tromer_pcd_paper", "label": "Chiesa-Tromer, Proof-Carrying Data (ICS 2010)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_bctv_curve_cycles_paper", "label": "BCTV, Scalable ZK via Cycles of Elliptic Curves (CRYPTO 2014)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_bcms_accumulation_paper", "label": "BCMS, PCD from Accumulation Schemes (TCC 2020)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recursion_recursion_outline_nova_paper", "label": "Kothapalli-Setty-Tzialla, Nova (CRYPTO 2022)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "recursion/recursion-outline.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id"